2. Temperature: The synthesis temperature affects the crystallinity and pore size of the zeolite. Higher temperatures can lead to larger crystal sizes and more uniform pore structures.

3. pH: The pH of the reaction mixture can influence the pore size and the shape of the zeolite.

4. Additives: The use of additives, such as additives, can help control the pore size, shape, and pore size of the zeolite.

5. Post-synthesis treatments: Post-treatment methods, such as acid or heat treatment, can be used to improve the properties of the zeolite.

