   - **Thezetization:** Silica nanoparticles in water tend to lose protons (OH-) from their surface, leading to a negatively charged surface. This is due to the formation of the Si-OH or Si-O-H groups on the surface, which can deprotonate to form Si-O- and H+ at neutral and alkaline pH values.
