### a. Spectral structure  
For a spiral system, the system is only functional if all components are functional.  
Thus, the system's reliability is the product of the individual compositions' resistance:  
\[
R_S(t) = R_1(t) \times R_2(t) \times \ldots \times R_n(t) = \prod_{i = 1}^{n} R_i(t)
\]  
This is because the system is only feasible when all components are feasible.  

**Example:**  
If the system has two components in spiral, \( R_1(t) = e^{-λ_1 t} \) and \( R_2(t) = e^{-λ_2 t} \), then:  
\[
R_S(t) = e^{-λ_1 t} \times e^{-λ_2 t} = e^{-(λ_1 + λ_2) t}
\]  

###. B. Personal storage document  
For a periodic system, the system is only feasible if at least one component is feasible.  
The system's reliability is 1 minus the probability that all components are false (optional):  
\[
R_S(t) = 1 - P(\text{all components are false (optional)}} = 1 - \prod_{i =1}^{n} (1 - R_i(t)) = 1 - \prod_{i = 1}^{n} S_i(t)
\]  
