","When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is mixed with a solution containing \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{Ti}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions in an acidified aqueous solution, the presence of \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) causes the formation of metal sulfides. The solubility of these sulfides depends on their \( K_{sp} \) values.

1. **\( \text{Mn}^{2+} \):** \( \text{Mn}^{2+} \) reacts with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) to form \( \text{MnS} \). The \( K_{sp} \) of \( \text{MnS} \) is \( 2.9 \times 10^{-16} \). This is a sparingly soluble compound, so it will precipitate.

2. **\( \text{Ni}^{2+} \):** \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \) reacts with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) to form \( \text{NiS} \). The \( K_{sp} \) of \( \text{NiS} \) is \( 3.0 \times 10^{-16} \). This is also a sparingly soluble compound, so it will precipitate.

3. **\( \text{Cu}^{2+} \):** \( \text{Cu}^{2+} \) reacts with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) to form \( \text{CuS} \). The \( K_{sp} \) of \( \text{CuS} \). is \( 8.3 \times 10^{-11} \). This is insoluble in acidic solution and precipitates.

4. **\( \text{Hg}^{2+} \):** \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) reacts with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) to form \( \text{H}_2\text{HgS} \), which is insoluble in water. The \( K_{sp} \) is negligible. This precipitate is white and dark when exposed to light.

Thus, all \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions will precipitate as their sulphides.

**Final Answer:**
The sulfides that precipitate are \( \text{MnS}, \text{NiS}, \text{CuS}, \) and \( \text{Hg}_2\text{S} \).",fluency,"# Task Description
