","The organic carbon fraction (\(t_o\)) is the most empirical relationship for the \(^{137}\text{Ce}\) transfer factor (TF) from soil to polluted rain water. The \(T_f\) is calculated as:
\[
T_f = \frac{C_t}{C_s} = \frac{1}{w_s + k_w}
\]
where \(C_t\) and \(C_s\) are the concentrations in the polluted rainwater and soil, \(w_s\) is the the ratio of water to soil, and \(k_w\) is the sorption coefficient of \(^{137}\text{Ce}\) to the soil.

The relationship between \(k_w\) and \(t_o\) is:
\[
k_w = \frac{1}{k_o}
\]
where \(k_o\) is the partition coefficient of \(^{137}\text{Ce}\) to organic carbon.

The relationship between \(k_o\) and \(t_o\) is:
\[
k_o = \frac{2.25 \times 10^{11}}{t_o}
\]
Substituting \(k_w\) into the \(T_f\) equation:
\[
T_f = \frac{C_t}{C_s} = \frac{1}{w_s + \frac{1}{k_o}} = \frac{1}{w_s + \frac{1}{\frac{2.25 \times 10^{11}}{t_o}} = \frac{1}{w_s + \frac{t_o}{2.25 \times 10^{11}} \cdot 10^{-11}}
\]
\[
T_f = \frac{1}{w_s + \frac{t_o}{2.25 \times 10^{11}} \times 10^{-11}}
\]

The average value of \(t_o\) for soil is \(0.01\) to \(0.02\). The average value of \(w_s\) is \(10\). The average value of \(t_o\) is \(0.015\). Substituting these values:
\[
T_f = \frac{1}{10 + \frac{0.015}{2.25 \times 10^{11}} \times 10^{-11}} = \frac{1}{10 + 6.67 \times 10^{-15}} \approx \frac{1}{10} = 0.1
\]

The empirical relationship for \(^{137}\text{Ce}\) transfer factor (TF) from soil to polluted rainwater is:
\[
\text{T-f} = \frac{1}{10 + \frac{f_o}{2.2 \times 10^{11}} \times 10^{-11}}
\]
where \(f_o\) is the fraction of organic carbon in the soil. The average value of \(f_o\) is \(0.015\). Substituting this value:
\[
