   The amplitude of \( 3\sin(2x + \frac{\pi}{4}) \) is \( 3 \).  
   The amplitude of \( -2\cos(3x - \frac{\pi}{3}) \) is \( 2 \).  
   The amplitude of the combined function is the sum of the individual amplitudes, which is \( 3 + 2 = 5 \).  

