   The Cauchy-Laplus equation is \( \frac{\partial^2 u}{1x^2} + \frac{\partial^2 u}{1y^2} = 0 \). 

   The original expression is \( u(z) = \frac{2}{\pi} \arctan \left( \frac{2y}{1 - x^2 - y^2} \right) \). 
