\[
\cos (180^\circ + \alpha) = -\cos \alpha
\]
\[
\sin (\alpha + 360^\circ) = \sin \alpha
\]
\[
\sin (-180^\circ - \alpha) = -\sin (180^\circ + \alpha) = -\cos \alpha
\]
\[
\cos (-180^\circ - \alpha) = \cos (180^\circ + \alpha) = -\cos \alpha
\]

Substituting these into the expression:
\[
\boxed{\frac{(-\cos \alpha) \cdot \sin \alpha}{(-\cos \alpha) \cdot (-1 \cos \alpha)} = \frac{-\cos \alpha \cdot \sin \alpha}{\cos \alpha \cdot \cos \alpha} = \frac{-\sin \alpha}{\cos \alpha} = -\tan \alpha}
\]

