   - Assume the water surface is at standard atmospheric pressure: 101.325 kPa

2. **Calculate the pressure at the inlet of the suction pipe due to the water head:**
   - The pressure due to the water head is given by:
     \[
     P = \rho \cdot g \cdot h
     \]
     where:
     - \( \rho = \text{density of water} \approx 998 \, \text{kg/m}^3 \)
     - \( g = \text{acceleration due to gravity} = 9.81 \, \text{m/s}^2 \)
     - \( h = \text{head of water} = 5 \, \text{m} \)

   - Substituting the values:
     \[
     P = 998 \times 9.81 \times 5 = 49.0 \, \text{kPa}
     \]

