\[
\text{Total momentum} = m_{\text{bullet}} v_{\text{bullet}} + m_{\text{Earth}} v_{\text{Earth}} = 0
\]

Rearranging to solve for \(v_{\text{Earth}}\):

\[
m_{\text{Earth}} v_{\text{Airth}} = - m_{\text{bullet}} v_{\text{bullet}}
\]
\[
v_{\text{Earth}} = -\frac{m_{\text{bullet}} v_{\text{bullet}}}{m_{\text{Earth}}}
\]

Substituting the given values:

\[
v_{\text{Earth}} = -\frac{(1 \text{ kg})(90.0 \text{ m/s})}{5.97 \times 10^{24} \text{ kg}} = -\frac{90.0}{5.97 \times 10^{24}} \text{ m/s} \approx -1.51 \times 10^{-22} \text{ m/s}
\]

The angular sign indicates the direction of the velocity (opposite to the projectile's vector). The magnitude of the velocity is:

\[

v_{\text{Earth}} \approx 1.51 \times 10^{-22} \text{ m/s}
\]

The correct answer is \(\boxed{1.51 \times 10^{-22} \text{ m/s}}\).
