q = flow rate (cm³ min⁻¹),
A = cross-sectional area of the tube (cm²)

First, we need to convert the diameter to radius:

Radius (r) = diameter / 2 = 0.1 mm / 2 = 0.05 mm = 0.005 cm

Now, we can calculate the cross-sectional area:

