\]
The time derivative is:
\[
\frac{dI_1(t)}{dt} = - \omega I_{1,\text{rms}} \sin(\omega t)
\]
Substituting into the current equation for coil 2:
\[
I_2 = \frac{1}{R_2} \left( \frac{\mu_0 N_1 N_2 A}{\ell} \right) \omega I_{1,\text{rms}} \sin(\omega t)
\]
The rms value of the current in coil 2 is:
\[
